==============================================================================
 PART H.  kappa honesty + summary
==============================================================================
[H1] kappa=1/2 is NOT forced by this construction. The functional F(s) is fixed by matching
     2F'(x^2)=mu_fw(x), which contains a0 as the only scale; kappa enters only through
     a0 = c H_L/Z with Z=2*kernel, kernel=sqrt(8pi/3), and the free-fall 1/2 = kappa. The
     in-in construction reproduces the SHAPE mu_fw and the BTFR coefficient combination GMa0,
     but a0 (hence Z, hence kappa) is an INPUT to the matching, not an output. kappa FREE. [HONEST]

[H2] SUMMARY (both ways):
   - mu_fw IS the Deser-Levin inertia ratio: EXACT identity [A3].
   - The conservative time-nonlocal MI functional is CONSTRUCTED explicitly in Galley
     doubled in-in form: S=S_phys[q+]-S_phys[q-], S_phys with non-quadratic kinetic F(s) [E].
   - Its EOM reproduces m*mu_fw(|a|/a0)*a=F [E3] and gives v^4=GMa0 exactly [F2].
   - It is CONSERVATIVE: W_loop=0 and <F.v>=0 at ALL amplitudes incl deep-MOND [G1,G2].
   - THE CRUX (both ways): the inversion mu(0)<mu(inf) does NOT come for free from
     'reactive instead of dissipative'. It requires a Foster-VIOLATING reactive residue
     (R<0) [D1], the lossless mirror of the X2 negative-absorption no-go. The functional is
     CONSERVATIVE (energy-conserving over a cycle) but NOT PASSIVE (its non-convex kinetic
     F encodes a reactive element the dS/Lambda sector must supply). [D2,E5]
   - kappa FREE [H1].
